# clinical v1.19 — clinical:CoverageTypeVocabularyShape, the value of
# clinical:coverageType on the DEPRECATED spelling.
#
# WHY THIS IS A .WARN. FIXTURE AND NOT A .INVALID. ONE. The severity follows the
# BINDING STRENGTH of the FHIR element the data was converted from, which is the
# rule coverage v1.4 established and clinical v1.19 copied unchanged. FHIR binds
# Coverage.type EXTENSIBLY, so a payer's local code is conformant at source: it
# is worth flagging for review and is not grounds for rejecting the record. A
# .INVALID. fixture here would assert a rejection the specification deliberately
# does not perform, and would fail with NO_VIOLATION.
#
# WHY IT IS NOT A .VALID. FIXTURE EITHER. .VALID. asserts only the absence of a
# violation, which this record also satisfies — and would therefore pass whether
# or not clinical:CoverageTypeVocabularyShape existed at all. That is the vacuous
# pass this repository exists to catch. .WARN. states the actual claim: the shape
# FIRES, at Warning severity, on a value outside the set.
#
# WHY THE SHAPE EXISTS. Through clinical v1.18 the value of this predicate was
# unconstrained, on the reading that the ontology comment ("medical, dental,
# vision, prescription, mental_health") and the corpus ("primary") disagreed and
# neither could be preferred without evidence. v1.19 corrected that: coverage
# v1.4 had already ratified a value set for this exact field, grounded in the
# FHIR binding, and it lists "primary" by name. Three of the comment's five
# values are accepted nowhere in this specification. The list here is
# coverage:CoverageTypeVocabularyShape's, copied unchanged, deliberately — the
# two predicates are the deprecated and the current spelling of ONE field, and a
# record should not be judged differently for which spelling it happens to carry.
#
# "commercial" is the realistic wrong value: it is the word payer systems, EOBs
# and member portals use for employer-sponsored coverage, and an importer that
# passes the payer's own vocabulary through writes it. It is in neither the
# retained Cascade values (primary, secondary, dental, vision) nor the v3-ActCode
# list. The nearest listed code is "EHCPOL".
#
# EVERYTHING ELSE HERE MUST BE CLEAN, or the fixture proves nothing: a .WARN.
# fixture that also violates something is rejected outright and is not evidence
# about the warning. clinical:CoverageRecordShape has FIVE constraints that can
# report at sh:Violation, not three. Three carry sh:severity sh:Violation
# explicitly — providerName, memberId, coverageType PRESENCE — and two more
# declare no sh:severity at all, which in SHACL means the default, and the
# default is sh:Violation: cascade:dataProvenance (sh:in, sh:minCount 1,
# sh:maxCount 1) and cascade:schemaVersion (sh:datatype, sh:minCount 1,
# sh:maxCount 1, sh:pattern major.minor). All five are satisfied below, which
# is why this record reaches the warning at all.
#
# CARRY THE LAST TWO ACROSS if you write a sibling fixture from this comment as
# the checklist. They are easy to miss precisely because the shape does not
# spell their severity out: dropping cascade:schemaVersion, or writing "1.3.0"
# where the pattern wants "1.3", produces a violation, and a .WARN. fixture
# that violates anything fails outright — with nothing in this header to say
# why. The value being wrong is the only thing wrong here.
#
# Fully synthetic: invented payer, member and group numbers.

@prefix cascade: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/core/v1#> .
@prefix clinical: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/clinical/v1#> .
@prefix health: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/health/v1#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<urn:uuid:c0vr-3eaa-4c9b-8f01-aabbccdd0003> a clinical:CoverageRecord ;
    clinical:providerName "Kestrel Mutual Health" ;
    clinical:memberId "KM-40118823" ;
    clinical:groupNumber "GRP-77120" ;
    clinical:planName "Kestrel Select PPO" ;
    clinical:planType "ppo" ;
    clinical:coverageType "commercial" ;
    clinical:relationship "self" ;
    clinical:effectivePeriodStart "2020-01-01T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    clinical:subscriberId "KM-40118823" ;
    cascade:dataProvenance cascade:ClinicalGenerated ;
    cascade:schemaVersion "1.3" ;
    health:sourceRecordId "ehr-coverage-2020-0101-003" .
